<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE language>
<!--
    hlsl.xml — Kate syntax definition for the shaders ShaderPlayer compiles.

    Structurally derived from KSyntaxHighlighting's own data/syntax/glsl.xml, with the
    word lists replaced by Shader Model 5.0 pixel-shader HLSL.

    Two deliberate omissions, both for the same reason: a definition that colours a name
    as an intrinsic advertises a function the compiler will reject.
      - atanh (and asinh/acosh) are NOT ps_5_0 intrinsics; fxc answers X3004. See the
        HLSL gotchas in CLAUDE.md for the hand-rolled replacement.
      - noise() parses but is not implemented for ps_5_0.

    The "ISF Block" context covers the leading /*{ ... }*/ parameter declaration that
    ShaderManager::ParseISFParams reads. It is a comment to fxc and the authoritative
    parameter list to this application, so it gets its own attribute and reads as a
    distinct recessed region rather than as one more comment.

    Beyond Normal there are exactly four contexts: the ISF block, a line comment, a block
    comment and a string. Preprocessor directives are matched in place instead, which
    leaves the body of a `#define Name custom[0].x` highlighted as the HLSL it expands to.
-->
<language name="HLSL"
          section="3D"
          extensions="*.hlsl;*.fx;*.ps"
          mimetype="text/x-hlsl"
          version="1"
          kateversion="5.0"
          author="ShaderPlayer"
          license="MIT"
          indenter="cstyle">
